      "confidence": 0.8,
      "curator_note": "Secondary fragmentation of the m/z-42 propene radical cation: radical-site alpha cleavage expels a hydrogen atom (.H) and forms the resonance-stabilised allyl cation C3H5+ (m/z 41, 10%). The precursor is encoded in its CH3-CH(.)-CH2+ localisation (radical on C2, charge on C3); one C1-H (H9) is made explicit as the bond that breaks. Book draws 0 electron-pushing arcs: Eq. 8.2 is a thermochemical fragmentation map (log k printed above each reaction arrow, heats of formation printed below each species), not a curved-arrow figure. All electron moves here are curator-inferred from the mechanism-type label printed under the reaction arrow; none is drawn on the page. Canonical THREE fishhooks: move<1> C2 odd electron into the forming C1=C2 pi bond; move<2> one C1-H9 electron completes C1=C2; move<3> the other C1-H9 electron onto H9 (the departing H atom)."
    },
